  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d56f9b50-0e17-50d2-be63-6256df5c6c7f" activityNameId="b0a3baba-d4b5-5cb8-a4ff-cd857180d1e8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Limestone, at mine</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Limestone, at mine
Land-use for recultivation has been included; size partition of dust emissions adapted from bauxite mining. The value for the module are normalized using a capacity of about 380'000 tons of product per year.;
CAS number: 001317-65-3; 
Formula: CaCO3; 
UUID: 696f7ad4-9824-3c6a-ada5-eabe8d9aa544
Includes blasting, all transports within the mine (for mining and recultivation), a part of the heating energy for "administration" buildings and the infrastructure. The land-use of the mine is included, the land-use of the paved roads and buildings within the mine are included in the module "mine, limestone". Output of overburden material neglected as it is only about 0.26% of mined limestone.
Location: data are only from one company in Switzerland (KFN), for some exchanges GLO-modules have been used as proxy
Technology: The company works on a technically high level; heavy machinery are operated electrically, building machines with diesel. Explosives used: Tovex at bottom and Amolith in shaft of drilled hole
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: survey 
Extrapolations: data which are only available for GLO have been used as proxy for CH
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_696f7ad4-9824-3c6a-ada5-eabe8d9aa544.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
